# Nautilus DevOps AWS Multi-Tier Infrastructure

This Terraform configuration provisions foundational AWS messaging, storage, and configuration management resources for the Nautilus DevOps cloud-native application stack.

## Architecture & Provisioned Resources

* **Amazon DynamoDB (`aws_dynamodb_table.app_table`):** Provisions the `devops-app-table` using on-demand (`PAY_PER_REQUEST`) capacity and a string partition key (`id`).
* **Amazon SNS (`aws_sns_topic.app_topic`):** Sets up the `devops-app-topic` for decoupled application messaging and notifications.
* **AWS SSM Parameter Store (`aws_ssm_parameter.app_config`):** Securely stores sensitive application configuration under `/devops/app/config` using `SecureString` encryption.

## Prerequisites

* Terraform v1.x+
* AWS Provider `~> 5.91.0`
* Valid AWS credentials configured in the environment

## File Structure

```text
/home/bob/terraform/
├── main.tf           # Core AWS resource definitions (DynamoDB, SNS, SSM)
├── variables.tf      # Input variable declarations
├── terraform.tfvars  # Environment-specific variable values
├── outputs.tf        # Exported resource names and ARNs
└── provider.tf       # AWS provider configuration
Input Variables
Name	Description	Type	Value (dev)
KKE_ENVIRONMENT	Target deployment environment	string	"dev"
KKE_DYNAMODB_TABLE_NAME	Name of the DynamoDB table	string	"devops-app-table"
KKE_SNS_TOPIC_NAME	Name of the SNS topic	string	"devops-app-topic"
KKE_SSM_PARAM_NAME	Path/name of the SSM parameter	string	"/devops/app/config"
Outputs
Name	Description
kke_dynamodb_table_name	Name of the provisioned DynamoDB table
kke_sns_topic_arn	ARN of the created SNS topic
kke_ssm_parameter_name	Name of the created SSM parameter
Usage
Bash
# Initialize the working directory and download providers
terraform init

# Preview infrastructure changes
terraform plan

# Apply the configuration
terraform apply -auto-approve

